--- !u!114 &2807600766462087685
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 8659458948632641698}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 04c6d700cc67f4b749d07401c724530f, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::SpaceGame.World.WorkshopGatekeeper
  arriveRadius: 1.2
  greetRadius: 14
  focusSeconds: 4
  hearingRadius: 30
  secondsPerLine: 4
  callOut: Hey! You there! Over here - please!
  plea:
  - Thank the tides, somebody came! Raiders - a whole gang of them - broke into our
    workshop last night!
  - On their way out they smashed the gate's gear train and threw the gears all over
    the sand. Now it won't open!
  - My family's shut in there and I'm stuck out here. Please, help me get the gate
    open!
  - Put the loose gears back on the pegs. When the chain of gears reaches the lock,
    it lets go.
  hints:
  - A gear that meshes with a turning one turns too. Follow the chain across to the
    lock on the other leaf.
  - '{gears} still lying in the sand. Every one of them belongs on that gate.'
  - If a gear won't go on, it would hit its neighbour. Try another peg.
  opened:
  - It's moving - you did it! The gate's open!
  - Come inside, quick - my family's in the main hall. I'll meet you in the middle!
  gathering:
  - Come on, come on - the middle of the main hall!
  briefing:
  - Everyone - this is the one who opened the gate!
  - But the raiders took something worse than our gate. They stole the Heart Gear
    - the big brass cog that drives this whole workshop.
  - Without it nothing down here will run for long. They can't have got far with
    a cog that heavy.
  - They went out through the gate. Find their trail out there - your scanner will
    pick up anything they dropped.
  - Track them down and bring the Heart Gear home. We'll be waiting right here.
  hunting:
  - Start at the gate and follow what they dropped. Your scanner will pick it up.
  - Careful. They're armed, and they won't hand it back nicely. If they spot you,
    whoever has the gear will run.
  carrying:
  - Is that - the Heart Gear! Bring it here, quick!
  thanks:
  - The Heart Gear! You brought it home!
  - We owe you more than we can say. Our workshop is yours to walk whenever you like.
  vaultOffer:
  - And that ship of yours - we can help you fix it.
  - 'We kept one part that fits a ship like yours: a sealed reactor core, locked
    away in our vault. We can install it for you.'
  - But you'll have to find the vault. It's hidden deep in the caves, behind the
    turning rooms.
  - Turn this main room with its big hand cog and the hidden hallways open up. From
    there, turn each room to find the way through.
  - Bring the core back, take it up to the crane console on the third floor, hang
    it on the hook and lower it onto your ship. We'll bolt it in.
  vaultHints:
  - The vault lies past the turning rooms. Turn the main room to face a new hallway,
    and follow it in.
  - Every room has its own hand cog. Hold it and the room turns; its doorway stays
    wherever you leave it.
  - The vault door has a little gear lock. The missing cogs are kept on the bench
    beside it.
  - That core is far too heavy to bolt on by hand. The hoist does it - work it from
    the console on the third floor.
  carryingCore:
  - That's the core! Up to the crane console on the third floor - bring the hook
    over and hang it on.
  coreOnHook:
  - Now lower it onto your ship's reactor mount. The console shows you where it goes
    - then let go.
  repaired:
  - There - it's in! Your ship has its reactor core back.
  - Safe travels, friend. Our workshop is yours whenever you need it.
  afterwards:
  - Thanks to you, the old place runs again.
  - Come back any time, friend.
  paceRadius: 2.5
  paceSpeed: 1.4
  callRadius: 14
